disclaude.md:5231:Explore-mapped (definitive): NOT a product snapshot-flush race (the product snapshot faithfully holds the agent's true final bytes; raising 15→45s had no effect because on-disk is already stable-and-correct). It's a HARNESS expected-sha derivation bug: build_soak _agent_declared_expected (disco_api.py:1559-1643) reconstructs each declared file's FINAL sha from the event log using an INCOMPLETE tool model — _FILE_WRITE_FULL_TOOLS={file_write} and _FILE_WRITE_PARTIAL_TOOLS omitted exact_replace + safe_write_file. In revise_thrice the model is steered to exact_replace for targeted follow-up edits (files.py:1345); when a revision's FINAL touch is exact_replace/safe_write_file, that op is invisible → 'expected' pins to an EARLIER file_write sha → permanent mismatch vs the correct latest snapshot bytes → false WORKSPACE_SNAPSHOT_NOT_READY (fatal 'sha' class, disco_api.py:1067). FIX (committed): safe_write_file→FULL (writes args.content verbatim → sha-precise), exact_replace→PARTIAL (→present_unproven, accepted best-effort). Verified end-to-end by the re-soak (no unit-test scaffold exists for this internal fn; the soak is the honest proof).
